.TH CBMAP_ALLOC 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
cbmap_alloc \- Memory allocation and management functions for CBMap

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/cbmap_internal.h>

.IB #include <lib/memalign.h>
.IB #include <lib/byte.h>
.IB #include <lib/str.h>

.IB double
.IB cbmap_mem_allocated (void);

.IB int
.IB cbmap_mem_memalign (void** p, size_t alignment, size_t size);

.IB void*
.IB cbmap_mem_debug_calloc (size_t count, size_t size, const char* file, int line);

.IB char*
.IB cbmap_mem_debug_strndup (const char* p, size_t size, const char* file, int line);

.IB char*
.IB cbmap_mem_debug_strdup (const char* p, const char* file, int line);

.IB void*
.IB cbmap_mem_mem_dup (const void* p, size_t size, const char* file, int line);

.IB void
.IB cbmap_mem_debug_free (const void* ptr, const char* file, int line);

.IB int
.IB cbmap_mem_posix_memalign (void** memptr, size_t alignment, size_t size, const char* file, int line);

.IB void
.IB cbmap_mem_debug_mem (const char* file, int line);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcbmap_alloc\fR library provides memory allocation and management functions specifically designed for use with CBMap. These functions include allocation, deallocation, and memory debugging features.

The functions provided by this library are:
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_allocated
Returns the total number of bytes allocated by the library.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_memalign
Allocates memory aligned to a specified alignment boundary.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_debug_calloc
Allocates memory for an array and initializes it to zero, with debugging information.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_debug_strndup
Duplicates a string up to a specified length, with debugging information.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_debug_strdup
Duplicates a string, with debugging information.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_mem_dup
Duplicates a block of memory, with debugging information.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_debug_free
Frees memory allocated by the library, with debugging information.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_posix_memalign
Allocates memory aligned to a specified alignment boundary using POSIX functions, with debugging information.
.TP
.B cbmap_mem_debug_mem
Logs the current allocation and deallocation status, with debugging information.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcbmap_alloc\fR library to allocate and free memory:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/cbmap_internal.h>
#include <lib/memalign.h>
#include <lib/byte.h>
#include <lib/str.h>

int main() {
    void* ptr;
    int result;

    // Allocate aligned memory
    result = cbmap_mem_memalign(&ptr, 64, 1024);
    if (result == 0) {
        printf("Memory allocated at %p\n", ptr);
        // Use the memory
        byte_copy(ptr, 1024, "example data");
        // Free the memory
        cbmap_mem_debug_free(ptr, __FILE__, __LINE__);
    } else {
        printf("Memory allocation failed\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
.nef